ion. They know how to make a gallon of paint last a month. Twice now they have been found sitting upright in the dark, not on watch — just watching. Breathing slow. When spoken to they said they couldn't sleep. Their eyes said otherwise. Eduardo grew up in Toledo, cornfields, lake wind, and rust-belt factory towns. Ashanti, Eduardo's friend, owed Eduardo twenty dollars since forever. Eduardo learned butchery with Ashanti, every November, deer season. The spring the levy vote failed and everybody knew what came next — before the sky, before all of this. Eduardo was there. Eduardo laughed the day the sky changed. Eduardo has never forgiven themself for it. Eduardo keeps coming back to one thing: keep these people fed through winter.","personality":{"temperament":"bold","sharing":"communal","curiosity":"methodical","quirk":"sits awake some nights just watching the others sleep","habit":"sleeps in short shifts","hope":"to sleep without dreaming","dark":{"kind":"malicious","tell":"sleep_watcher"}},"age":49,"goal":"feed","intelligence":{"primary":"creative","secondary":"steady"},"abilityWeights":{"care":1,"fieldcraft":2,"system":2},"items":["seed_packet","hard_candy","buskers_harmonica","trail_compass","dog_tags"],"talk":["\"Someone has to stay hopeful, right? Might as well be me. I'm good at faking it till it's real.\"","\"My street artist training covered a lot. 'Post-apocalyptic foraging' was not on the syllabus.\"","\"You know what's weird? I'm a street artist — was a street artist — and none of that prepared me for any of this.\""],"quest":["You're awake. Don't sit up fast — you were out a full day. Woke up wanting to sleep without dreaming.","I woke up in a clearing with eleven strangers and one a street artist — me. First thing I did was count heads — old street artist habit, I guess. All I wanted was to sleep without dreaming.","We have to decide — Eduardo says together, or starving separately. I'm a street artist, not a leader, but someone has to say it.","I'm Ed